# Steadfast canonical line-ending policy — SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH.
# Root-fix 2026-08-06 (GAP-79): made uniform across ALL repos + the sf-init template,
# from the proven CastForge FEATURE-laptop-perfect policy (2026-04-26). Every repo
# carries an identical copy of this file (vendored from here) and was renormalized once
# (`git add --renormalize`). Enforced by gate-line-endings.
#
# WHY: without a policy, files show as phantom-"modified" across machines because
# autocrlf converts endings differently per checkout (the SMOKEY<->SMOKESTACK churn,
# GAP-10). With this, all text is LF in the working tree everywhere, so the two
# machines agree byte-for-byte. Code moves between machines via git remotes, never by
# Syncthing copying the .git folder (see .stignore + TETHER-CONTINUITY.md).

# All text files: LF in the working tree on every OS (kills the autocrlf trap).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows scripts must stay CRLF (cmd.exe / PowerShell / wscript have LF edge cases).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.vbs text eol=crlf

# POSIX shell / git hooks stay LF regardless of platform.
*.sh text eol=lf

# sops-encrypted files travel as raw bytes — never convert (breaks the HMAC check).
*.sops.env  -text
*.sops.json -text
*.sops.yaml -text
release-secrets.sops.env -text
